  "principles": [
    "The riff is the rhythm section — drop-C palm-muted pedal tones in minor/Phrygian, double-tracked L/R (identical in breakdowns, varied in verses, octave-split in choruses); kick and bass lock to the chugs",
    "Double-kick, skank and gallop drumming at 130-170 BPM in verses, opening to a crash-driven backbeat under the clean chorus",
    "Good cop / bad cop — screamed riff verses vs. a clean, melodic chorus over i-VI-III-VII with power chords ringing",
    "Half-time breakdown as the climax, set up by a stop — kick doubles the chugs, snare on 3, china on quarters, space between hits"
  ],
