  "research_sources": [
    "https://metalcoredeathcorehardcoregrindcore.fandom.com/wiki/Breakdowns?oldid=3972 (breakdowns: open low strings, drop D-drop B, half-time, snare on 3, kick follows chugs)",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heavy_metal_drumming (blast beats with double bass; ride part moved to crash/china; breakdown quarter-note china; cymbal chokes)",
    "https://www.riffhard.com/?p=37226 (clean melodic chorus after heavy verse; I-IV-V / vi-IV-I-V)",
    "https://tunee.ai/music-generator/metalcore (BPM ranges: 120-170 general, 130-170 melodic metalcore)",
    "https://guitarmasterclass.net/ls/Killswitch-Engage-Style2 (KsE-style lesson: drop B, B minor, 120 BPM)",
    "https://medium.com/p/b137a6de5f49 (double-bass programming: 16th kicks under 2-and-4 snare)",
    "https://eprints.soton.ac.uk/496107 (breakdown treated as a distinct formal section)",
    "https://github.com/crunkkid411/metalerator (pedal-tone riff rules, verse root motions, kick-follows-guitar breakdowns, form incl. stop / pre-breakdown / final chorus)",
    "https://solemntones.com/products/odin-iii and https://solemntones.com/pages/faq (Odin III articulations, non-latching keyswitches, tuning range)",
    "https://www.nailthemix.com/have-you-tried-programmed-guitars-solemn-tones-odin-is-here (Swift Mode velocity → articulation)",
    "http://www.godprobe.com/projects/notemaps/ (Toontrack default drum note map)",
    "https://www.prosoundweb.com/in-the-studio-techniques-for-double-tracking-guitars/ (two performances panned L/R) and https://homerecording.com/bbs/threads/quad-tracking-guitars.334378/ (octave chords / different voicings on one side)"
  ],
